#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128785 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de55bc-23b5-574c-9fab-33c4bca720fe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia About a Perpendicular Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "915a7c2d-3797-5dfa-8d68-85e2546a23d6" :question/math-academy-id "e-11778" :question/problem "Consider a plane lamina of mass $2\\,\\textrm{kg}$ and center of mass $(0,1),$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $2.5\\,\\textrm{kg}\\cdot\\textrm{m}^2,$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through the point $(2,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line $l_M$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to $l_M$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = I_M + d^2M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and $I_M$ and $I_l$ are the moments of inertia about the lines $l_M$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the line through the center of mass $(0,1)$ and the line through the point $(2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(2-0)^{2}+(1-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =2.5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.5+8 \\\\  & =10.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $10.5\\,\\mathrm{kg}\\cdot\\mathrm{m^2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128786 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "850f196a-9607-56c2-b0a7-a00d4d5a4741" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia About a Perpendicular Axis Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/id #uuid "153b828d-545a-58fb-bc81-0d7311726a87" :question/math-academy-id "e-11779" :question/problem "Calculate the moment of inertia of a circular plate that occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $1\\,\\textrm{m}$ with mass density $\\lambda(x, y) =2(x^2+y^2),$ measured in $\\textrm{kg}/\\textrm{m}^2,$ about a line perpendicular to the disk passing through a point on the circumference." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line $l_M$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to $l_M$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = I_M + d^2M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and $I_M$ and $I_l$ are the moments of inertia about the lines $l_M$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (r,\\theta) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq r \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq \\theta \\lt 2\\pi \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nSince the mass density is symmetric in $x$ and $y,$ $D$'s center of mass is at $(0,0).$ The mass density function, in polar coordinates, is given by $\\lambda(r,\\theta) = 2r^2.$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{r}^{2}\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{1}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\pi \\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{r}^{2}\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{1}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line passing through a point on the circumference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+{1}^{2}\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128799 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5c774e2-7c3f-56a9-99b6-96aca1cd4f49" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Parallel Axes"}] :question/id #uuid "72ccaeab-ad76-50c7-8b51-7736c5270521" :question/math-academy-id "e-12493" :question/problem "A circular plate of mass $2 \\, \\textrm{kg}$ with uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $4 \\, \\textrm{m}$ and is centered at the origin.\nGiven that the moment of inertia of the plate about a line $l$ perpendicular to the plate is $24 \\, \\textrm{kg} \\cdot \\textrm{m}^2,$ find the distance of the line $l$ from the center of mass of $D.$" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line $l_M$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to $l_M$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = I_M + d^2M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and $I_M$ and $I_l$ are the moments of inertia about the lines $l_M$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (r,\\theta) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq r \\leq 4, \\: 0 \\leq \\theta \\lt 2\\pi \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $\\mathcal{A} = \\pi \\cdot 4^2 = 16\\pi\\,\\textrm{m}^2.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(r,\\theta) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{2}{16\\pi} = \\dfrac{1}{8\\pi}\\,\\textrm{kg}/\\textrm{m}^2,\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{4}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\pi }\\cdot 64\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ 24 & =16+2{d}^{2} \\\\ 2{d}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =4 \\\\ d & =2\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128800 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f203c5-4866-5077-9ef9-0d2122581c4f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia of a Rectangular Plate About a Perpendicular Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "131948d9-d533-5316-bcd3-b7859244892e" :question/math-academy-id "e-12494" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $3\\,\\textrm{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\le x \\le 2, \\: 0 \\le y \\le 4 \\big\\},$\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters.\nFind the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $1\\,\\textrm{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line $l_M$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to $l_M$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = I_M + d^2M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and $I_M$ and $I_l$ are the moments of inertia about the lines $l_M$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $\\mathcal{A} = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\\,\\textrm{m}^2.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{3}8\\,\\textrm{kg}/\\textrm{m}^2,\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid:\n\n$$\n\\left(\\bar{x},\\bar{y}\\right) = \\left( \\dfrac{0+2}2, \\dfrac{0+4}2 \\right) = (1,2)\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{¯}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{¯}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{3}{8}((x-1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}3(x-1)^{2}+3(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3(x-1)^{2}y+(y-2)^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{0}^{2}12(x-1)^{2}+16\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{[4(x-1)^{3}+16x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(4+32-(-4+0)) \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $1\\,\\textrm{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =5+{1}^{2}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f203c5-4866-5077-9ef9-0d2122581c4f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia of a Rectangular Plate About a Perpendicular Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "405db70d-d40f-5e2e-9152-8ebb91470814" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370991} {:answer/id #uuid "3c64760d-c517-5f94-b9ad-04a905be0e59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{44}{15}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370992} {:answer/id #uuid "c05424b5-db70-50b5-bf5b-dcdb39137ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{5}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370993} {:answer/id #uuid "eb946f56-103a-575d-a3fd-f268f346b802" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370994} {:answer/id #uuid "1c91722d-14d6-547a-bae3-be799272b3b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{15}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c64760d-c517-5f94-b9ad-04a905be0e59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{44}{15}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370992} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d938f87-ae50-59b4-a944-653d39f85756" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370990}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f66a0c3f-e290-5a0d-824c-35593ff13ee1" :question/math-academy-id "q-163172" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $\\frac{4}{5}\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-2\\le y\\le 2},$\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 4=8\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{(\\frac{4}{5})}{8}=\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid:\n\n$$\n(\\overset{¯}{x},\\overset{¯}{y})=(\\frac{-1+1}{2},\\frac{-2+2}{2})=(0,0)\n$$\n\nSince the center of mass is at the origin, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\frac{1}{10}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=-2}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}4{x}^{2}+\\frac{16}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{[\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{16}{3}x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{32}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(\\frac{40}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{8}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{44}{15}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129484 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "850f196a-9607-56c2-b0a7-a00d4d5a4741" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia About a Perpendicular Axis Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9fcd119-7b1c-5963-b717-027ffaf46b38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370997} {:answer/id #uuid "0fa3e045-2608-56ce-9ec8-4290a68ba291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370998} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5b5bfb-6116-5fe6-864e-3ddc0c6bf1f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370999} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f91532-c065-55fe-8ab5-1233527e7930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371000} {:answer/id #uuid "6f5c6974-42c0-5d49-ac48-0b7b73f369b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fa3e045-2608-56ce-9ec8-4290a68ba291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370998} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b7e4605-11fa-53ab-bc68-514fa9de2146" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370996}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c746d262-efcf-5fbe-a185-059c81fe24fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-163213" :question/problem "A circular plate of mass $2\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $2\\,\\text{m}$ centered at the origin.\nFind the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $4\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $A=\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}=4\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{2}{4\\pi }=\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot 4\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $4\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =4+{4}^{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4+32 \\\\  & =36\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "850f196a-9607-56c2-b0a7-a00d4d5a4741" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia About a Perpendicular Axis Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41364da5-362e-5e3d-a139-7667a7fc74bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371004} {:answer/id #uuid "faeb1880-bb61-5344-839d-4938fb454db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "68\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371005} {:answer/id #uuid "52de5ab6-a461-59d4-b865-e70439212765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371006} {:answer/id #uuid "11de8378-dd48-5bd8-940a-790b5c113599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "59\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371007} {:answer/id #uuid "127ffe31-bf77-5cb2-8948-ca06f997302f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52de5ab6-a461-59d4-b865-e70439212765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371006} :answer-field/id #uuid "b142a173-af6f-51e9-b688-acab8f826063" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1630a7cf-2bba-567b-8908-484b6a319c97" :question/math-academy-id "q-163815" :question/problem "A circular plate of mass $8\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $4\\,\\text{m}$ centered at the origin.\nFind the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $0.5\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $A=\\pi \\cdot {4}^{2}=16\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{8}{16\\pi }=\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{4}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\cdot 64\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =64\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $0.5\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =64+{0.5}^{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =64+2 \\\\  & =66\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371009 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "850f196a-9607-56c2-b0a7-a00d4d5a4741" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia About a Perpendicular Axis Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "615f0a6e-b81e-5e25-b9f3-a43da06c5536" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi (3{e}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371011} {:answer/id #uuid "3a2761ab-d57d-5885-9ff1-ec02000cb240" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi {e}^{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371012} {:answer/id #uuid "406cf5c2-633e-519e-8c28-9943b9e437ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi e\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371013} {:answer/id #uuid "0a5ee5e7-7b88-5657-bcab-4eb0134ea291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi (5{e}^{3}-3e)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371014} {:answer/id #uuid "8054fc12-eb1e-5fb0-9d23-7db655c7d9a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi (9{e}^{3}-5e)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8054fc12-eb1e-5fb0-9d23-7db655c7d9a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi (9{e}^{3}-5e)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371015} :answer-field/id #uuid "f603edcc-90d9-5144-8191-32235531fa66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e12fb34d-0332-5ccb-be57-aaeab4b67e58" :question/math-academy-id "q-163819" :question/problem "Calculate the moment of inertia of a circular plate that occupies the region of an annulus $D$ centered at $O$ with inner radius $1\\,\\text{m},$ outer radius $3\\,\\text{m},$ and mass density \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}},\n$$\n\n measured in $\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ about a line perpendicular to the ring passing through a point $2\\,\\text{m}$ from its center.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n\\int {t}^{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t=({t}^{2}-2t+2){e}^{t}+C\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nSince the mass density is symmetric in $x$ and $y,$ the center of mass is at $(0,0).$ The mass density function, in polar coordinates, is given by \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{{e}^{r}}{r}.\n$$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{e}^{r}}{r}\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{e}^{r}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={e}^{r}{|}_{1}^{3}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =({e}^{3}-e)\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi ({e}^{3}-e)\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{e}^{r}}{r}\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{2}{e}^{r}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =({r}^{2}-2r+2){e}^{r}{|}_{1}^{3}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =(5{e}^{3}-e)\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi (5{e}^{3}-e)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $2\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =2\\pi (5{e}^{3}-e)+{2}^{2}\\cdot 2\\pi ({e}^{3}-e) \\\\  & =2\\pi (9{e}^{3}-5e)\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371016 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de55bc-23b5-574c-9fab-33c4bca720fe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia About a Perpendicular Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f816ddb1-fd7c-5f47-b92b-4098f8068e2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.56\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371018} {:answer/id #uuid "991dad0e-bf43-5256-a293-fbcf2df2ecd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371019} {:answer/id #uuid "803864dd-e042-50af-9308-74a92e10b888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.25\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371020} {:answer/id #uuid "28a6a55a-08b5-576e-9bdd-d4fc1bf93bd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.45\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371021} {:answer/id #uuid "b9230374-38ce-58f4-9c5e-b0590e6c06f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.75\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371022}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f816ddb1-fd7c-5f47-b92b-4098f8068e2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.56\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371018} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f14ff89-3d8d-5a32-ba4c-3de349e8ab2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371017}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e74ffb9c-da8a-5ca1-b0a6-2aca5d2c0cf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-163820" :question/problem "Consider a plane lamina of mass $4\\,\\text{kg}.$ If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $1.75\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through a point on the lamina at a distance of $45\\,\\text{cm}$ from its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the lines is $d=45\\,\\text{cm}=0.45\\,\\text{m}.$ Then, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =1.75+(0.45)^{2}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1.75+0.81 \\\\  & =2.56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $2.56\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de55bc-23b5-574c-9fab-33c4bca720fe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia About a Perpendicular Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07268289-02e5-523b-97df-06069c6e575b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16.25\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371025} {:answer/id #uuid "d2deecd8-df33-595e-a8c5-282938148b8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21.24\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371026} {:answer/id #uuid "944d533c-bd30-53c4-a326-a824fc0b60ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.84\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371027} {:answer/id #uuid "0cc5776b-6706-518f-b518-34f1ce1d9899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24.32\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371028} {:answer/id #uuid "2bf5d6af-fc26-556a-a311-436e31b353c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28.21\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2deecd8-df33-595e-a8c5-282938148b8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21.24\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371026} :answer-field/id #uuid "c80d312c-2921-55b3-a9b7-43238ef65456" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76c6f959-207b-5481-9a1c-b735876c24e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-163822" :question/problem "Consider a plane lamina of mass $6\\,\\text{kg}.$ If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $12.6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through a point on the lamina at a distance of $1.2\\,\\text{m}$ from its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the lines is $d=1.2\\,\\text{m}.$ Then, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =12.6+(1.2)^{2}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12.6+8.64 \\\\  & =21.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $21.24\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de55bc-23b5-574c-9fab-33c4bca720fe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia About a Perpendicular Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eba6ce7-a431-5b10-8cb2-7e64b2b21983" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.52\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371032} {:answer/id #uuid "b2308af4-cd22-56ae-955b-5f3c191ff06e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.24\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371033} {:answer/id #uuid "ad8d5e38-1d2a-5c54-9ae2-4ff0c67c562f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.25\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371034} {:answer/id #uuid "294e1fad-9fb1-5a2c-9c7b-6c915adaa441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.05\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371035} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e6f040-05e8-5fa4-99b9-23fe571f1d04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.55\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "294e1fad-9fb1-5a2c-9c7b-6c915adaa441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.05\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371035} :answer-field/id #uuid "1013b314-94ca-5efe-b71b-53112dbe327c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d290f4cc-58df-55ec-8f34-6793b9bc5d8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163824" :question/problem "Consider a plane lamina of mass $1\\,\\text{kg}.$ If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $0.8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through a point on the lamina at a distance of $1.5\\,\\text{m}$ from its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the lines is $d=1.5\\,\\text{m}.$ Then, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =0.8+(1.5)^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0.8+2.25 \\\\  & =3.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $3.05\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de55bc-23b5-574c-9fab-33c4bca720fe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia About a Perpendicular Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a876db2a-bd63-54e5-8635-3ec253de5748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.1\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371039} {:answer/id #uuid "b2fc490d-fb6d-5338-95e7-a5b75e680903" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.3\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371040} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2bcc4f-77d7-5644-91f5-c198913a0200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.4\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371041} {:answer/id #uuid "aadc1052-5531-55f8-8a25-c0072491c583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.8\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371042} {:answer/id #uuid "dadde9ac-f5ca-5ab0-b234-f43871dd2904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9.6\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b2bcc4f-77d7-5644-91f5-c198913a0200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8.4\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371041} :answer-field/id #uuid "8db2c00e-700d-5060-995f-06579c8a5e38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93bd2469-9a25-513c-ace8-46c089b4cef1" :question/math-academy-id "q-163827" :question/problem "Consider a plane lamina of mass $0.8\\,\\text{kg}$ and center of mass $(3,1),$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through the point $(1,-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the line through the center of mass $(3,1)$ and the line through the point $(1,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(3-1)^{2}+(1-(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =2+(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}\\cdot 0.8 \\\\  & =2+6.4 \\\\  & =8.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $8.4\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de55bc-23b5-574c-9fab-33c4bca720fe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia About a Perpendicular Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e448a7ea-57f2-5d5b-a4bc-ba36ab309867" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72.5\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371046} {:answer/id #uuid "0ee989cc-cc03-5ac9-8b24-8b554c120b84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64.2\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371047} {:answer/id #uuid "21c44c9b-e157-563d-9b64-c82a3b006372" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52.3\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371048} {:answer/id #uuid "6301779e-228b-58e2-891a-36a2f9dfeda1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56.4\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371049} {:answer/id #uuid "764e4c09-8e1e-5a10-9c37-887a9c951ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "67.2\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "764e4c09-8e1e-5a10-9c37-887a9c951ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "67.2\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371050} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d985965-e7b5-5c82-96c5-027595a3c69f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c6b89a9a-3bc8-52bb-9308-67e5bb47736e" :question/math-academy-id "q-163829" :question/problem "Consider a plane lamina of mass $8\\,\\text{kg}$ and center of mass $(4,1),$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. If the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass is $3.2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ what is the moment of inertia of the lamina about an axis parallel to the first passing through the point $(2,-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe distance between the line through the center of mass $(4,1)$ and the line through the point $(2,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(2-4)^{2}+(-1-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =3.2+(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =3.2+64 \\\\  & =67.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $67.2\\,kg\\cdot {m}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371051 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5c774e2-7c3f-56a9-99b6-96aca1cd4f49" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Parallel Axes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7447dc25-8ae7-5746-a7c2-2a0dabedcb67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371053} {:answer/id #uuid "c11bc0e5-04a8-587b-9443-8c3bf83efc7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371054} {:answer/id #uuid "37191f11-a1b0-5f59-838e-5091bd444511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371055} {:answer/id #uuid "014a7187-6c78-56dc-b144-14e757b24c7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371056} {:answer/id #uuid "801a8f44-1ff6-50fd-b843-71f2cd84fc07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c11bc0e5-04a8-587b-9443-8c3bf83efc7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371054} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba48e99b-ff5d-5759-a3b9-6cce867b11fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39a8451a-e3d3-5731-af49-8935d7153d2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-164128" :question/problem "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina of mass $6\\,\\text{kg}$ about the perpendicular line passing through its center of mass is $4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nIf the moment of inertia of the same lamina about another perpendicular line is $7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ find the distance between the two lines." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nApplying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ 7 & =4+6{d}^{2} \\\\ 6{d}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ d & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance between the two axes is $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,m.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371058 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5c774e2-7c3f-56a9-99b6-96aca1cd4f49" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Parallel Axes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abc54ca4-99a2-594a-9089-7675437dda99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371060} {:answer/id #uuid "f7fecd53-fcab-588c-abeb-ec8178516014" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371061} {:answer/id #uuid "139d3597-f54b-5789-bb5d-1e85bca114a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371062} {:answer/id #uuid "2ad807ef-5374-540e-ab78-17c02b660e3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371063} {:answer/id #uuid "70e148ec-35da-5a90-a0ff-e675d7ae7bbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ad807ef-5374-540e-ab78-17c02b660e3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371063} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d108581-aed1-5e62-8db5-99c95c1c2e27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f2a3b6db-d90c-5461-809c-963135152c4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-164130" :question/problem "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ about the perpendicular line passing through its center of mass is $5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nIf the moment of inertia of the same lamina about another perpendicular line is $\\frac{35}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ find the distance between the two lines." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nApplying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ \\frac{35}{4} & =5+3{d}^{2} \\\\ 3{d}^{2} & =\\frac{15}{4} \\\\ {d}^{2} & =\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ d & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance between the two axes is $\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\,m.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5c774e2-7c3f-56a9-99b6-96aca1cd4f49" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Parallel Axes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f454e89-7e0d-53da-a3f8-9fb81193bbe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371067} {:answer/id #uuid "af7021f8-514d-57c9-9fbf-45016d944d5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371068} {:answer/id #uuid "655dd2f5-b9d7-53ab-b6d6-3e94ecfd6338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371069} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb8701a-3ac2-5a90-a691-683cc4ad5cb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371070} {:answer/id #uuid "e3f22964-09ea-58a0-b7d0-7ad0ac4e1525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "655dd2f5-b9d7-53ab-b6d6-3e94ecfd6338" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371069} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a697e8a-ee01-5b65-80be-564b4bc36819" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b1269dc-9a9c-5e0c-a19a-b98eb7ba6d4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-164132" :question/problem "A circular plate of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ with uniform mass density occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $2\\,\\text{m}$ and is centered at the origin.\nGiven that the moment of inertia of the plate about a line $l$ perpendicular to the plate is $15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ find the distance of the line $l$ from the center of mass of $D.$" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nThe area of the circular plate $D$ is $A=\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}=4\\pi \\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{3}{4\\pi }\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid $(0,0).$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{2}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4\\pi }\\cdot 4\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ 15 & =6+3{d}^{2} \\\\ 3{d}^{2} & =9 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =3 \\\\ d & =\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371072 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f203c5-4866-5077-9ef9-0d2122581c4f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia of a Rectangular Plate About a Perpendicular Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc67ea13-e505-5710-95aa-88f5cae81889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371074} {:answer/id #uuid "61cec991-4bb5-5f08-8a74-27460a1eb888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371075} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3e7559-432b-5fe3-94a5-4f6a37e20fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371076} {:answer/id #uuid "c47508ca-16e1-5310-9c56-77d369c8d7f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371077} {:answer/id #uuid "3ae32a9a-572f-5af8-8f41-9772417945e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed3e7559-432b-5fe3-94a5-4f6a37e20fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371076} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fab4b4c-9a97-52e8-a49f-ff96da129d68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f49fba6-7f94-5351-9dc9-902caa762884" :question/math-academy-id "q-164139" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $\\frac{6}{5}\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-3\\le y\\le 3},$\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 6=12\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{(\\frac{6}{5})}{12}=\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid:\n\n$$\n(\\overset{¯}{x},\\overset{¯}{y})=(\\frac{-1+1}{2},\\frac{-3+3}{2})=(0,0)\n$$\n\nSince the center of mass is at the origin, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{1}{10}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=-3}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}6{x}^{2}+18\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}{[2{x}^{3}+18x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}(4+36) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot 40 \\\\  & =4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =4+(\\sqrt{5})^{2}\\cdot \\frac{6}{5} \\\\  & =4+6 \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371079 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f203c5-4866-5077-9ef9-0d2122581c4f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia of a Rectangular Plate About a Perpendicular Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edcbe783-8ea2-5a7c-902f-7860021f07d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371081} {:answer/id #uuid "87dbd094-0420-5e9e-9a13-fcdb704784f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371082} {:answer/id #uuid "77fab254-abef-5bb3-9a98-359cc1181887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371083} {:answer/id #uuid "49e497bb-34a3-5a2d-8f76-73906f70b41c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371084} {:answer/id #uuid "eabd2d1b-5816-5055-88b5-11ac3a1206f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edcbe783-8ea2-5a7c-902f-7860021f07d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371081} :answer-field/id #uuid "73a70246-904d-5645-a681-4052a444af21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92d2cf38-4289-5f99-9071-595327e42a3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-164140" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $3\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1},$\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=4\\cdot 2=8\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{3}{8}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid:\n\n$$\n(\\overset{¯}{x},\\overset{¯}{y})=(\\frac{-2+2}{2},\\frac{-1+1}{2})=(0,0)\n$$\n\nSince the center of mass is at the origin, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=-1}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}2{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{2}{3}x]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}(\\frac{32}{3}+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}(\\frac{40}{3}) \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =5+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =5+\\frac{3}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371086 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f203c5-4866-5077-9ef9-0d2122581c4f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia of a Rectangular Plate About a Perpendicular Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6969c5dc-fb91-5e6c-962f-675f76bf1900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371088} {:answer/id #uuid "38aedf87-a4ea-514a-ba49-90457e1da599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371089} {:answer/id #uuid "fb7d6c83-dcda-5df5-a279-9f981c6acde7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371090} {:answer/id #uuid "f519448a-79b9-5a33-b21a-e73321bbdae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371091} {:answer/id #uuid "1ec6ced8-295f-535e-805e-e76483d880de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb7d6c83-dcda-5df5-a279-9f981c6acde7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371090} :answer-field/id #uuid "59688c65-cd58-5be1-af7b-456937335ff2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371087}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "677a6071-7ce4-5abc-a513-660a8ad8e603" :question/math-academy-id "q-164142" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2},$\nwhere $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters.\nFind the moment of inertia of the plate about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{(\\frac{3}{2})}{4}=\\frac{3}{8}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid:\n\n$$\n(\\overset{¯}{x},\\overset{¯}{y})=(\\frac{-1+1}{2},\\frac{0+2}{2})=(0,1)\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{¯}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{¯}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}+3(y-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[3{x}^{2}y+(y-1)^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}6{x}^{2}+2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{[2{x}^{3}+2x]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(2+2-(-2-2)) \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =1+{(\\sqrt{6})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =1+9 \\\\  & =10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371093 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f203c5-4866-5077-9ef9-0d2122581c4f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia of a Rectangular Plate About a Perpendicular Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "361e12ef-d36f-5091-a2cc-8ee80ea91c4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371095} {:answer/id #uuid "2d9deb71-da79-55ca-bb22-387d464533d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371096} {:answer/id #uuid "d2ff6b21-311f-55d1-98c1-b58c8ccad1f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371097} {:answer/id #uuid "f34899c2-97e4-5bde-88bf-76bec5c42d12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371098} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f8f65e-8706-57ff-a37f-6f24f683d2af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "361e12ef-d36f-5091-a2cc-8ee80ea91c4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371095} :answer-field/id #uuid "2283c62b-039c-5d8e-801d-3a4068c40aac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371094}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fb6e2375-c7b1-5f37-b50b-167a66de4a06" :question/math-academy-id "q-164147" :question/problem "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}$\nand has mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x,$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters.\nGiven that the center of mass is at $(2,1),$ find the moment of inertia about a line perpendicular to $D$ at a distance of $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,\\text{m}$ from a parallel line passing through its center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{3}\\cdot y{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =9\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass $(2,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{¯}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{¯}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}((x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}((x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2})2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2x(x-2)^{2}+2x(y-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[2x(x-2)^{2}y+\\frac{2}{3}x(y-1)^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4x(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+16x+\\frac{4}{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+\\frac{52}{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}-\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{26}{3}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =81-144+78-0 \\\\  & =15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =15+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})}^{2}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =15+4 \\\\  & =19\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371100 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5c774e2-7c3f-56a9-99b6-96aca1cd4f49" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Parallel Axes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b6b9860-ada7-59ef-a471-769725a3eecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371102} {:answer/id #uuid "06575fb5-2bce-55f1-b3da-a6f0b9dc51e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371103} {:answer/id #uuid "98a03c3e-1561-5693-81b3-2f91c8fd8c27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371104} {:answer/id #uuid "6a1ba289-a9c8-5201-a1e5-2184124d5b53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371105} {:answer/id #uuid "201055b1-f61f-5d7e-906d-da6bdbf1e1d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371106}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98a03c3e-1561-5693-81b3-2f91c8fd8c27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371104} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1cd0802-1f4a-5f5c-9beb-7ddab9580bfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2530e161-4473-52c3-bf05-108490fabea7" :question/math-academy-id "q-164149" :question/problem "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}$\nand has mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=4xy,$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. The moment of inertia of the plate about a line $l$ perpendicular to the plate is $\\frac{16}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nGiven that the center of mass of the plate is at $(2,\\frac{2}{3}),$ find the distance of the line $l$ from the center of mass." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =9\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass $(2,\\frac{2}{3})$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}((x-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}+(y-\\overset{―}{y})^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}((x-2)^{2}+{(y-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}((x-2)^{2}+{(y-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2})\\cdot 4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x(x-2)^{2}y+x{y}^{3}-\\frac{4}{3}x{y}^{2}+\\frac{4}{9}xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{2}x(x-2)^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}x{y}^{4}-\\frac{4}{9}x{y}^{3}+\\frac{2}{9}x{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}x(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{4}{9}x+\\frac{2}{9}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{73}{36}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{[\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{4}-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{73}{72}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{81}{8}-18+\\frac{73}{8}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{5}{4} \\\\  & =5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ \\frac{16}{3} & =5+9{d}^{2} \\\\ 9{d}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ {d}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{27} \\\\ d & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ d & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371107 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "850f196a-9607-56c2-b0a7-a00d4d5a4741" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia About a Perpendicular Axis Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bda7dceb-313c-5af3-839f-5654021acd43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371109} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0bd479-bb12-59b2-b127-3805ca37e55f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371110} {:answer/id #uuid "5d79ff77-8aee-500f-a4e7-08b2b91f9ce5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371111} {:answer/id #uuid "2b99eb1e-404a-5655-a7f9-e1da0ed4bea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371112} {:answer/id #uuid "ccc27c94-f833-5dfc-8eed-18d48d858cba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{4}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371113}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d79ff77-8aee-500f-a4e7-08b2b91f9ce5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371111} :answer-field/id #uuid "89233c8d-9c1c-539e-ac0b-1775bb43481d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c3e82248-046d-51ec-a301-4e2c4f12e087" :question/math-academy-id "q-164409" :question/problem "Calculate the moment of inertia of a circular plate that occupies the region of an annulus $D$ centered at $O$ with inner radius $1\\,\\text{m},$ outer radius $\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m},$ and mass density $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{|xy|}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},$ measured in $\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ about a line perpendicular to the ring passing through a point $3\\,\\text{m}$ from its center." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nSince the mass density is symmetric in $x$ and $y,$ the center of mass is at $(0,0).$ The mass density function, in polar coordinates, is given by \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{|r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta |}{{r}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|.\n$$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{r}^{2}{|}_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2-1)\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{1}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(4-1)\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $3\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+{3}^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+9 \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129609 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5c774e2-7c3f-56a9-99b6-96aca1cd4f49" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Parallel Axes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afa7e64c-96de-50b2-b1e7-6c32cf02af47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.32m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127449} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e959a5-d581-5f29-bd74-c1154c3447db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.64m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127450} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca02970-463a-549d-ad88-86c6d0cf87fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.05m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127451} {:answer/id #uuid "3263e975-58d3-5093-a360-be70e7ae7fdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127452} {:answer/id #uuid "46b8fc3a-a442-5ea8-a338-dd225e7a32c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afa7e64c-96de-50b2-b1e7-6c32cf02af47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.32m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127449} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f951b7a-3145-5300-b033-a10775914546" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5901650d-61bf-5ba0-9311-6334934249d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-38584" :question/problem "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina of mass $0.5\\,\\text{kg}$ about the perpendicular line passing through its center of mass is $0.2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nIf the moment of inertia of the same lamina about another perpendicular line is $0.25\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2},$ find the distance between the two lines. Round your final answer to two decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nApplying the parallel axis theorem and solving for $d,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\ 0.25 & =0.2+0.5{d}^{2} \\\\ 0.5{d}^{2} & =0.05 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =0.1 \\\\ d & =0.316\\,22….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance between the two axes is $0.32\\,m,$ rounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371114 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "850f196a-9607-56c2-b0a7-a00d4d5a4741" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Moment of Inertia About a Perpendicular Axis Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38315fe3-f714-57e6-bf09-d988b60d413c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371116} {:answer/id #uuid "38d7f0e4-01b0-5718-95f8-006d835cd658" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371117} {:answer/id #uuid "3a6ef0eb-0346-5387-b6ac-0fe054c21f56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371118} {:answer/id #uuid "9b0e57e7-152d-5031-a1cb-c821e22e8abc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371119} {:answer/id #uuid "32264ac7-500b-5bbc-bea7-cda54c8a6686" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a6ef0eb-0346-5387-b6ac-0fe054c21f56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371118} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f74e85b-0d83-5528-b6d3-e84f09bb1db7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b73e87d-4517-5d33-b6a8-a5f0a1bd251a" :question/math-academy-id "q-38587" :question/problem "Calculate the moment of inertia of a circular plate that occupies the region of a disk $D$ of radius $\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}$ with mass density $\\lambda (x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2},$ measured in $\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ about a line perpendicular to the disk passing through a point on the circumference." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nSince the mass density is symmetric in $x$ and $y,$ its center of mass is at $(0,0).$ The mass density function, in polar coordinates, is given by $\\lambda (r,\\theta )={r}^{2}.$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{2}\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =2\\pi \\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{2}\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line passing through a point on the circumference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}+{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}+4\\pi  \\\\  & =\\frac{20\\pi }{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
